{"t":1377866.8151633,"req":"h01","event":"done","status":"answered","level":0,"steps":["classify","retrieve","draft"],"answer":"The original attention mechanism divides the query\u2011key dot products by a constant (specifically \\(1/\\sqrt{d_k}\\)) before applying softmax to prevent the dot products from becoming too large as the dimensionality \\(d_k\\) grows, which would push the softmax into regions with extremely small gradients. This scaling keeps the values in a range where the softmax is more stable and trainable. [C:attention:9]"}
